      "message": "It doesn\u0027t seem to. Makefile.rules just has this:\n\ncmd_exe \u003d $(CC) $(ro-objs) $(HOST_TEST_LDFLAGS) $(LDFLAGS_EXTRA) -o $@\n\nI see a couple lines above, LDFLAGS has CFLAGS_CPU explicitly added. I could append $CFLAGS_CPU to HOST_TEST_LDFLAGS. Is that better? \n\nSome of the ideas seem confused here. We seem to have all three of the classic GCC build/host/(target) definitions, but smudge them together in a confusing way. Are we planning to be able to cross-compile the tests? If so, why are \"target\" variables like CFLAGS_CPU and LDFLAGS_EXTRA ending up in a final object that\u0027s linked with HOST_TEST_LDFLAGS? If we\u0027re not planning to cross-compile the tests, why is there a distinction between BUILD and HOST?\n\nAnyway I guess this will all go away someday anyway. Let me know what\u0027s correct here.",
